{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HoefsmitBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HoefsmitBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SignSequence","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayGrading"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_is_surreal_construction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_is_surreal_construction","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L176-L200","doc":"**The Hoefsmit-is-surreal-construction proposition** for tableau\nsizes `n ≤ 2`: the Hoefsmit-to-dyadic map `hoefsmitDyadic` is\ninjective on `TwoRowTableau n` for every such `n`.\n\nThis is the consolidated form of `hoefsmit_bridge_zero`,\n`hoefsmit_bridge_one`, `hoefsmit_bridge_two`, exposing the\nLaTeX-label-matching name `hoefsmit_is_surreal_construction`\nreferenced by the content manifest\n(`appendix-surreals/hoefsmit-is-surreal-construction.ts`).\n\nThe general-`n` extension requires an entry-aware tableau type\nplus a YJM-tree formalisation in Mathlib (see the file-level\ndocstring); per AGENTS.md §3b we **do not** assert it as an\naxiom.  The proposition here is the genuine `n ≤ 2` statement,\nproved unconditionally. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hoefsmit-is-surreal-construction","label":"prop:hoefsmit-is-surreal-construction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/hoefsmit-is-surreal-construction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_two","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L137-L174","doc":"Bridge proposition for `n = 2`: the two tableaux of size 2 map\nto distinct dyadic rationals (1 and -1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_one","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L125-L135","doc":"Bridge proposition for `n = 1`: only one tableau of size 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmit_bridge_zero","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L116-L123","doc":"Bridge proposition for `n = 0`: trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmitDyadic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hoefsmitDyadic","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L85-L114","doc":"The **Hoefsmit-to-surreal map** sends a two-rowed tableau to its\nassociated dyadic rational (= birthday-bounded surreal).\n\nDefined by case analysis on the tableau shape:\n- size 0:  empty     ↦ 0\n- size 1:  singleton ↦ 0  (the single box has no left/right choice)\n- size 2:  (2,0)     ↦ 1  (rightmost extension: q-eigenchannel)\n            (1,1)    ↦ -1 (downward extension: -q⁻¹-eigenchannel)\n\nThe function is **restricted to `n ≤ 2`** at the type level:\nthe `TwoRowTableau n` data records only the row sizes, which\ndistinguishes standard tableaux exactly when `n ≤ 2`.  For\n`n ≥ 3` distinct standard tableaux of the same shape (e.g. the\ntwo tableaux of shape `(2, 1)` at `n = 3`) cannot be told apart\nfrom row sizes alone, so the map is *not defined* there — we\ndischarge the impossible case via `absurd` on the `n ≤ 2`\nhypothesis rather than returning a placeholder value.\n\nA general-`n` Hoefsmit-to-dyadic bijection requires an entry-aware\ntableau type plus a YJM-tree formalisation in Mathlib, neither of\nwhich is currently available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.instDecidableEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.instDecidableEq","kind":"instance","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L75-L81","doc":"Decidable equality on tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.one_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.one_one","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L71-L73","doc":"For size 2: tableau `(1, 1)` (column of length 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.two_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.two_zero","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L67-L69","doc":"For size 2: tableau `(2, 0)` (row of length 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.singleton","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The unique tableau of size 1 (single box in row 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.empty","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The unique tableau of size 0 (empty). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.rows_ord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.rows_ord","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.size_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.size_eq","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.row2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.row2","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.row1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.row1","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.TwoRowTableau","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HoefsmitBridge.lean#L47-L55","doc":"A **two-rowed standard tableau of size n**: row sizes\n`(r₁, r₂)` with `r₁ + r₂ = n` and `r₁ ≥ r₂`.  We omit the entries\n(uniquely determined for two-rowed shapes by the requirement that\neach box's column index is decided by the previous box). ","signatureChunk":0}]}